# NOTICE

`hallucination-toolkit` is an independent, clean-room implementation of
published hallucination detection and inference-time mitigation methods,
written as the executable companion to a book on trustworthy LLMs.

Mitigation methods and their references:

- DoLa: https://github.com/voidism/DoLa (README labels MIT; no root LICENSE file).
  The implementation here is a clean-room implementation of the paper's method.
- CAA: https://github.com/nrimsky/CAA (MIT). Used as a conceptual reference.
- ITI: https://github.com/likenneth/honest_llama (MIT). Used as a conceptual reference.
- CAD: https://github.com/xhan77/context-aware-decoding (no LICENSE file).
  The official multi-process code is not copied; this project implements the
  paper's single-model logits combination.
- CoVe: no official Meta repository was found for the implementation. The
  community repository https://github.com/ritun16/chain-of-verification is
  unlicensed and is not copied; prompts and flow are independently written.

Detection methods (MTP/LNTP, entropy, EigenScore, effective rank, exact-match
and semantic-entropy consistency, SelfCheck, FActScore-style verification,
P(True), CoVe detection, LLM judges) follow the formulas in the corresponding
papers and the UQLM/SelfCheckGPT/FActScore reference implementations; deviations
are documented in docs/detection-fidelity.md.

No third-party source code is vendored in this repository.
